            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Socialize your baby. Your baby will need to spend time around other children of a similar and different age. This will help your child learn to interact and be around others. Set up play-dates so that your baby gets to spend playtime with a friend. [[Image:Care for Your New Baby Step 23.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Look out for colds. Colds are normal in small children and should not be a cause for concern. Usually they will go away from two weeks. However, if your child is younger than 2-3 months, go to doctor as this can result in more serious health conditions.[[Image:Care for Your New Baby Step 25.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Socialize your baby. Your baby will need to spend time around other children of a similar and different age. This will help your child learn to interact and be around others. Set up play-dates so that your baby gets to spend playtime with a friend. <ref>http://www.parenting.com/article/the-social-life-of-babies</ref>[[Image:Care for Your New Baby Step 23.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Look out for colds. Colds are normal in small children and should not be a cause for concern. Usually they will go away from two weeks. However, if your child is younger than 2-3 months, go to doctor as this can result in more serious health conditions.<ref>http://www.parenting.com/article/dr-sears-guide-to-the-top-7-infant-illnesses?page=0,1</ref>[[Image:Care for Your New Baby Step 25.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
