            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "deletion",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Don’t worry too much about the soft spot. Babies skulls will not fully close until they are roughly a year and a half to two years old.<ref>http://www.mayoclinic.com/health/healthy-baby/PR00043</ref> Until then, you will notice that there are soft spots on their head. Don’t worry too much, however. The membrane that covers these spots is very tough and your baby will be perfectly safe. You can touch these areas or comb the baby’s hair without causing any harm.[[Image:Care for Your New Baby Step 2.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Don’t worry too much about the soft spot. Babies skulls will not fully close until they are roughly a year and a half to two years old.<ref>http://www.mayoclinic.com/health/healthy-baby/PR00043</ref> Until then, you will notice that there are soft spots on their head. Don’t worry too much, however. Like seriously, you could push down as hard as you can and nothing will happen. The membrane that covers these spots is very tough and your baby will be perfectly safe. You can touch these areas or comb the baby’s hair without causing any harm.[[Image:Care for Your New Baby Step 2.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
        },
